1
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:03,780
There!

2
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:09,030
Another day of cleaning up all these
cigarette butts off the ground.

3
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:11,820
- What the hell?!
- Crap.

4
00:01:11,830 --> 00:01:13,920
I got tar juice on my clothes.

5
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:19,590
Yani Neko, what are you, nuts?!

6
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:24,850
Rent's not due until next week, right?

7
00:01:25,630 --> 00:01:26,630
Schwing!

8
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:29,730
Just be more careful from now on!

9
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:45,440
I just found a long ciggy butt!

10
00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:49,660
It's a little black
from some weird juice, though.

11
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:52,240
It'll be fine.

12
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:03,170
Damn it!

13
00:02:04,050 --> 00:02:07,930
That stupid, raunchy cat!

14
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:16,860
Why?!

15
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:52,490
BE MINDFUL OF YOUR SURROUNDINGS
TO AVOID EXPOSURE TO SECONDHAND SMOKE.

16
00:03:52,490 --> 00:03:54,530
SMOKING UNDER THE AGE OF 20
IS PROHIBITED BY LAW.

17
00:03:54,530 --> 00:03:56,530
A brand-new pack of smokes.

18
00:03:56,530 --> 00:04:01,450
But it's not in its complete form yet.

19
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:07,090
New packs are packed tight.

20
00:04:07,670 --> 00:04:09,840
When you take out about five, 

21
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:13,800
it leaves just enough room
to fit in a cheap lighter.

22
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:18,760
Nothing beats a pack of smokes like this.

23
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:34,240
Life in its perfect form is fleeting.

24
00:04:36,830 --> 00:04:40,130
It's packed so tight
that I can't get any out.

25
00:04:51,590 --> 00:04:52,550
Ain't no way.

26
00:04:53,130 --> 00:04:54,130
Just why?

27
00:04:54,630 --> 00:04:57,760
What did I do to deserve this?

28
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:00,810
Wait, three-second rule.

29
00:05:01,310 --> 00:05:04,230
I'll just take home the ones
that didn't land in shit.

30
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:07,690
Money's already tight this month.

31
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:16,780
They're probably fine
if I just cut off the tips.

32
00:05:17,370 --> 00:05:18,960
Chainsmoker Cat!

33
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:26,080
Okay, all anthro temps, 
can I have your attention?

34
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:28,040
Here's what you're doing today.

35
00:05:29,130 --> 00:05:32,260
And by the way, the entire facility
has a strict no-smoking policy.

36
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:34,640
Your cigarettes will be confiscated
until you clock out.

37
00:05:41,010 --> 00:05:43,300
After 20 minutes of no smoking, 

38
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:48,440
blood pressure and other vital signs
return to normal.

39
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:55,490
After 30 minutes of no smoking, 

40
00:05:55,490 --> 00:06:00,700
nicotine concentration in the body halves, 
and withdrawal symptoms begin to appear.

41
00:06:06,290 --> 00:06:09,460
After six to eight hours of no smoking, 

42
00:06:09,460 --> 00:06:15,220
carbon monoxide and oxygen concentration
in the blood return to normal levels.

43
00:06:18,430 --> 00:06:20,100
Where did number 56 go?

44
00:06:20,100 --> 00:06:21,310
She bolted!

45
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:23,470
She has 30 minutes left on her shift!

46
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:42,570
That's so good!

47
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:47,710
Are you the anthro helper?

48
00:06:47,710 --> 00:06:50,590
This vase is a national treasure.

49
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:52,290
I ask that you don't scratch it, 

50
00:06:52,290 --> 00:06:56,130
or get your beast smell all over it.

51
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:58,220
You got it.

52
00:07:15,610 --> 00:07:19,280
How is it even dirtier
than it was before you polished it?

53
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:24,500
Plus, it smells like a train station.

54
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:34,290
Curse you!

55
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:39,840
I have 170 yen to my name.

56
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:41,220
And six cigarettes.

57
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:44,930
There are six days left
until my next day job.

58
00:07:45,510 --> 00:07:48,310
I have to live off of 28 yen a day.

59
00:07:48,890 --> 00:07:51,430
And one cigarette a day.

60
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:55,820
Okay, it's doable!

61
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:01,400
This is my first and last cigarette
of the day.

62
00:08:06,370 --> 00:08:10,170
When I'm smoking, 
I'm freed from my worries.

63
00:08:10,910 --> 00:08:12,160
Yeah.

64
00:08:12,170 --> 00:08:16,800
Surviving six days on 170 yen is nothing.

65
00:08:22,430 --> 00:08:24,140
Okay, maybe just one more.

66
00:08:33,190 --> 00:08:35,690
Well, crap.

67
00:08:35,690 --> 00:08:39,440
You know, smoking just one a day
was gonna be too hard anyway.

68
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,980
Now that they're gone, 
I'll be able to accept it.

69
00:08:45,070 --> 00:08:47,280
Why does this always happen?

70
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:48,660
Always, always, always!

71
00:08:48,660 --> 00:08:51,250
Why is my willpower so shit?

72
00:08:51,830 --> 00:08:55,420
I'm not a bad person.

73
00:09:02,010 --> 00:09:06,010
God hasn't abandoned me yet!

74
00:09:06,010 --> 00:09:08,350
Your total is 1, 160 yen.

75
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:14,440
REMAINING FUNDS: 10 YEN

76
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:17,180
Chainsmoker Cat.

77
00:09:20,150 --> 00:09:22,190
Sis?

78
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:24,160
It's been a while.

79
00:09:24,150 --> 00:09:25,280
What's going on?

80
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:30,370
Nothing, just calling because I wanted
to hear my little sister's voice.

81
00:09:31,290 --> 00:09:32,330
You're weird.

82
00:09:32,910 --> 00:09:35,830
I miss you. It's been way too long.

83
00:09:35,830 --> 00:09:37,540
You should come hang out sometime.

84
00:09:37,540 --> 00:09:39,170
- No way.
- What?!

85
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,500
Your place always smells like cigarettes.

86
00:09:42,510 --> 00:09:44,680
I bet your floor is covered in ash.

87
00:09:44,670 --> 00:09:46,880
Of course not.

88
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:48,800
Then send me a pic of your room.

89
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:51,390
I'll consider coming over after I see it.

90
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:02,270
I'm going to clean this place up.

91
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,990
I'm going to do it.

92
00:10:04,690 --> 00:10:07,650
First, get the trash together.
No, I need trash bags before that.

93
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:08,910
What do I do with the floor?

94
00:10:08,910 --> 00:10:11,250
Gather the butts, 
throw them out, clean the fridge.

95
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:12,410
Clean the poop ring.

96
00:10:12,410 --> 00:10:14,580
I'm in so much trouble.

97
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:15,790
I'm running out of time!

98
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:25,970
It hurts.

99
00:10:25,970 --> 00:10:29,390
Why am I so unlucky?

100
00:10:29,390 --> 00:10:32,770
I need to smoke.

101
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:38,140
These are still totally smokable.

102
00:10:39,770 --> 00:10:43,770
This one hasn't been smoked!
Best day ever!

103
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:47,450
I'm so lucky.

104
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:52,950
It's Sis.

105
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:56,830
She must have scrambled to clean her room.

106
00:10:57,330 --> 00:11:00,500
I guess if it's just a little messy, 
I'm willing to overlook it.

107
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:01,420
LOOK, LITTLE SIS!

108
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,590
Poop.

109
00:11:08,170 --> 00:11:10,340
GO DIE

110
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:16,550
I think I'll try to stop smoking

111
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:19,270
since Little Sis seems mad.

112
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,280
That's way too many words.

113
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:30,950
I mean, 
the more I put on, the better, right?

114
00:11:42,630 --> 00:11:46,130
DO NOT TRY THIS AT HOME

115
00:11:46,130 --> 00:11:47,090
What?

116
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:51,300
Wow, you haven't smoked
for three whole days?

117
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:53,050
I'm just doing my best.

118
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:57,770
I mean, you were smoking so much, 
it's like you were running on nicotine.

119
00:11:57,770 --> 00:11:59,350
I'm so proud of you!

120
00:11:59,350 --> 00:12:01,270
You are?

121
00:12:01,270 --> 00:12:02,690
I'm serious!

122
00:12:02,690 --> 00:12:06,190
This is without a doubt the greatest thing
you've ever accomplished.

123
00:12:06,770 --> 00:12:08,480
Come on, you're praising me too much.

124
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:10,320
What?

125
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:30,550
Nothing beats beer
in the middle of a weekday.

126
00:12:37,310 --> 00:12:39,350
It's a heart-shaped smoke ring.

127
00:12:39,350 --> 00:12:42,060
That's gotta be a lucky sign.

128
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,320
Hey there.

129
00:12:49,610 --> 00:12:53,110
What do you want, Smoke-face?

130
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:58,950
Just sharing my good fortune.

131
00:13:05,210 --> 00:13:06,040
Hey.

132
00:13:07,710 --> 00:13:10,210
Go buy me some booze and smokes.

133
00:13:10,210 --> 00:13:11,750
Beer and Mild Seven.

134
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:15,220
But I need to do my homework.

135
00:13:15,890 --> 00:13:20,020
You talking back to me, boy?

136
00:13:20,010 --> 00:13:22,350
Stop your stupid studying!

137
00:13:22,350 --> 00:13:25,270
You're getting a job
right out of middle school anyway!

138
00:13:25,270 --> 00:13:26,360
But…

139
00:13:27,610 --> 00:13:31,740
You should be grateful
I take care of your ugly mug.

140
00:13:31,730 --> 00:13:36,280
Now show a little gratitude and go buy
my booze and cigarettes, you little shit.

141
00:13:42,290 --> 00:13:44,000
What's wrong?

142
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:03,600
Honestly.

143
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:08,610
What's with my sister and the landlord
ganging up on me, telling me I smell?

144
00:14:14,820 --> 00:14:20,780
Man, I hate showering.
What a pain in the ass.

145
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:41,220
But you know, despite everything, 
it does make me feel refreshed.

146
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:43,890
Baths are like laundry for your soul.

147
00:14:44,470 --> 00:14:47,970
Maybe I actually like being clean.

148
00:14:59,950 --> 00:15:01,830
Yeah, getting clean is a pain, 

149
00:15:01,820 --> 00:15:04,950
but I do love me a good smoke
after a bath.

150
00:15:18,510 --> 00:15:21,680
My throat hurts, and I have chills.

151
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:23,770
Could I have a cold?

152
00:15:26,390 --> 00:15:28,600
Yeah, this is definitely a cold.

153
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:32,060
The cigarettes taste so bad, 
I can't smoke at all.

154
00:15:32,770 --> 00:15:34,900
I need to rest.

155
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:46,620
Thank you, come again.

156
00:15:57,590 --> 00:16:00,510
Okay, I can at least manage
to smoke menthols.

157
00:16:25,950 --> 00:16:27,870
Help.

158
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:33,170
Why did you run away?

159
00:16:33,870 --> 00:16:36,250
I went out of my way to come nurse you.

160
00:16:36,250 --> 00:16:39,000
I thought you were someone
from Public Health.

161
00:16:39,010 --> 00:16:42,140
Normally, people don't come and nurse you
in a hazmat suit.

162
00:16:42,130 --> 00:16:45,090
That's because it smells like cigarettes, 

163
00:16:45,090 --> 00:16:47,880
and you never clean.

164
00:16:47,890 --> 00:16:51,270
I can't handle the combo of trash and tar.

165
00:16:52,890 --> 00:16:54,930
Anyway, how do you feel?

166
00:16:56,230 --> 00:16:58,070
A little better than yesterday.

167
00:17:02,150 --> 00:17:03,690
I'll make you some porridge.

168
00:17:05,109 --> 00:17:07,450
Her words may be harsh, 

169
00:17:08,030 --> 00:17:09,950
but she still came despite everything.

170
00:17:09,950 --> 00:17:13,200
My little sister loves me.

171
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:16,880
Porridge is done.

172
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:27,349
Oh my god, are you okay? I'm so sorry!

173
00:17:27,339 --> 00:17:29,090
Gross! No way!

174
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:31,600
Where's my mask? No, no, no!

175
00:17:37,770 --> 00:17:38,730
What the hell?

176
00:17:39,570 --> 00:17:40,650
What is this?

177
00:17:42,230 --> 00:17:43,940
Does it really smell that bad?

178
00:17:44,490 --> 00:17:47,330
Not gonna lie, that hurts.

179
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:50,620
THE PREVIOUS DAY

180
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:56,490
If it isn't Imoko.

181
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:58,750
Hello, Kansai.

182
00:17:59,630 --> 00:18:01,720
Thank you for everything you do
for my sister.

183
00:18:02,210 --> 00:18:03,840
You're so polite.

184
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:06,680
Are you really that thing's sister?

185
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:08,590
What're you doing?

186
00:18:08,590 --> 00:18:11,800
Apparently, my sister caught a cold.

187
00:18:11,810 --> 00:18:13,770
So, I came to buy a hazmat suit.

188
00:18:14,350 --> 00:18:17,730
I see, that's why you're here.

189
00:18:17,730 --> 00:18:20,730
Still, can't believe that thing gets sick.

190
00:18:20,730 --> 00:18:24,650
My sister has always been prone to colds.

191
00:18:24,650 --> 00:18:27,400
She'd do stuff like
eat 50 popsicles in one sitting.

192
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:30,070
Or jump into snow wearing a T-shirt.

193
00:18:30,660 --> 00:18:33,410
And every time, I take care of her.

194
00:18:33,410 --> 00:18:34,990
Sounds like a lot of work for you.

195
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,210
Tell me about it.

196
00:18:38,370 --> 00:18:40,580
It must be a hassle coming out this way.

197
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:42,710
I don't mind checking on her
if you shoot me a text.

198
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:47,720
Thank you.

199
00:18:48,430 --> 00:18:51,730
But nobody knows my sister better than me.

200
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:55,470
I think it's best if I'm the one
who takes care of her.

201
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:01,730
- So cute.
- So cute.

202
00:19:02,310 --> 00:19:03,730
Let me adopt you.

203
00:19:03,730 --> 00:19:05,270
Why?

204
00:19:06,610 --> 00:19:09,570
Chainsmoker Cat.

205
00:19:14,580 --> 00:19:17,580
Doctor, are my sister's lungs…

206
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:19,910
She is definitely going to die.

207
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:20,800
No!

208
00:19:21,290 --> 00:19:24,290
She has maybe two, three months left.

209
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:25,550
No!

210
00:19:25,550 --> 00:19:28,300
Well, maybe a little longer.

211
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:30,390
Around 100 days?

212
00:19:31,010 --> 00:19:32,340
One-hundred…

213
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:33,180
cats?

214
00:19:34,970 --> 00:19:36,220
Imoko!

215
00:19:36,850 --> 00:19:38,600
How dare you make my sister cry!

216
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:41,140
Your lungs are to blame.

217
00:19:41,940 --> 00:19:44,030
Look, I get it.

218
00:19:44,650 --> 00:19:46,320
Everybody dies eventually.

219
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:49,410
That's all there is to it.

220
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:56,780
No smoking inside the hospital, 
you filthy beast scum!

221
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:00,660
A dream?

222
00:20:00,660 --> 00:20:01,750
It was just a dream?

223
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:06,960
So the lung cancer and the 100 days left
to live were all just a dream?

224
00:20:14,140 --> 00:20:15,430
Sis?

225
00:20:15,430 --> 00:20:16,890
What's wrong?

226
00:20:16,890 --> 00:20:18,390
Did I wake you up?

227
00:20:18,390 --> 00:20:20,600
No, I was doing my homework.

228
00:20:21,890 --> 00:20:23,890
You sound kind of down.

229
00:20:23,900 --> 00:20:25,530
Did your cold come back?

230
00:20:28,650 --> 00:20:30,110
I'm fine.

231
00:20:31,650 --> 00:20:32,780
Really?

232
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:33,740
Yeah.

233
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:38,240
Really. It's nothing.

234
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:43,200
I just wanted to talk to you.

235
00:20:43,790 --> 00:20:45,250
Yeah?

236
00:20:45,250 --> 00:20:47,630
Anyway, you need to take care of yourself.

237
00:20:48,130 --> 00:20:51,680
It's not easy coming over
in a hazmat suit, you know?

238
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:54,550
Imoko.

239
00:20:54,550 --> 00:20:55,590
Yeah?

240
00:20:57,550 --> 00:21:00,390
I'm going to quit smoking, I swear!

241
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:08,150
Look outside. It's really pretty.

242
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:19,710
Amazing, isn't it?

243
00:21:20,490 --> 00:21:23,240
Apparently, the Milky Way
is really clear tonight.

244
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:26,540
I don't know what happened, 

245
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:29,670
but you can always call me
whenever you want.

246
00:21:35,090 --> 00:21:36,880
The stars are so pretty.

247
00:21:37,390 --> 00:21:38,470
Yeah.

248
00:21:39,100 --> 00:21:40,980
I'm right here

249
00:21:40,970 --> 00:21:42,600
under the same stars.

250
00:21:44,390 --> 00:21:46,980
It looks like cigarette smoke.

251
00:21:46,980 --> 00:21:47,860
What?

252
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,730
What was that sound?

253
00:21:50,730 --> 00:21:51,980
Sis?

254
00:21:51,980 --> 00:21:53,230
I heard a flick.

255
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:56,530
Was that a lighter?

256
00:21:56,530 --> 00:21:58,240
What did you just light?

257
00:21:58,240 --> 00:22:02,750
You said you were going to quit smoking!

258
00:22:04,910 --> 00:22:06,700
Man, that tastes good.

259
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:38,010
Subtitle translation by: Zensho Yamamoto

260
00:23:38,010 --> 00:23:38,930
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

261
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:40,920
UNDERAGE SMOKING AND DRINKING
IS PROHIBITED. DO NOT IMITATE.
